<title>USA: Strawbridge cuts distribution to holders.</title>
<headline>Strawbridge cuts distribution to holders.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strawbridge &amp; Clothier said Monday it cut the initial distribution of shares of May Department Stores Co to 0.20 of a share of May from 0.29.</p>
<p>It cut the initial distribution because it is facing a lawsuit by the landlord of the Shore Mall store seeking to block the entire distribution, it said.</p>
<p>The company agreed to give the landlord thirty days notice of any further distributions other than cash representing dividends received on the remaining May shares.</p>
<p>It also agreed not give that notice prior to September 15.</p>
</text>
